from pathlib import Path
import json, html
p=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
v=json.loads((p/'validation.json').read_text()); s=json.loads((p/'turn-study.json').read_text()); preserved=json.loads((p/'preservation.json').read_text())
f=lambda x: '—' if x is None else f'{x:.2f}'
esc=html.escape
pairs=lambda r,k: f"{f(r['current']['metrics'][k])} → <b>{f(r['candidate']['metrics'][k])}</b>"
tables=[]
for pace,title in [('jog','Jog · 3.0 m/s'),('run','Run · 5.5 m/s'),('sprint','Full sprint · 8.2 m/s')]:
    rows=[]
    for r in s['runs']:
        if r['pace']!=pace: continue
        cells=''.join(f'<td>{pairs(r,k)}</td>' for k in ['brakingDistance','maximumLateralExcursion','timeToFace','timeOntoNewLine','pathLength','pathRatio'])
        rows.append(f'<tr><td><a href="turns.html?angle={r["angle"]}&pace={pace}">{r["angle"]}° ↗</a></td>{cells}</tr>')
    tables.append(f'<h3>{title}</h3><div class="overflow"><table><thead><tr><th>Correction</th><th>Brake distance m</th><th>Max lateral m</th><th>Face s</th><th>On new line s</th><th>Path length m</th><th>Path / direct</th></tr></thead><tbody>{"".join(rows)}</tbody></table></div>')
# Validation summary includes the nine unchanged fixtures and exact resulting timestamps.
cases=v['scenarios'] if 'scenarios' in v else v.get('fixtures',v.get('runs',[]))
if not cases:
    cases=next(x for x in v.values() if isinstance(x,list) and x and isinstance(x[0],dict) and 'input' in x[0])
def outcome(x):
    return ('Received '+f(x['receive'])+' s') if x['receive'] is not None else ('Abandoned '+f(x['abandon'])+' s') if x['abandon'] is not None else x['outcome']
case_rows=''.join(f'<tr><td>{esc(r["id"])}</td><td>{outcome(r["current"])}</td><td>{outcome(r["candidate"])}</td></tr>' for r in cases)
terrible=next(r for r in cases if r['id']=='terrible')
events=''.join(f'<tr><td>{e["kind"].replace("_"," ")}</td><td>{e["time"]:.3f} s</td><td>{e["speed"]:.3f} m/s</td></tr>' for e in terrible['candidate']['events'])
page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Runner cuts · measurements</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css"><style>main{display:block;max-width:1180px}.card{margin:20px 0;padding:26px}.card p,.card li{font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;max-width:980px}h2{font-size:25px}h3{margin:26px 0 8px}.overflow{overflow-x:auto}table{width:100%}th,td{white-space:nowrap;padding:11px 9px;font-size:12px}td b{color:#165d49}.split{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.4fr 1fr;gap:28px}.callout{border-left:4px solid #b89249;background:#f5eedb;padding:16px 20px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6}.tag{font-weight:700;color:#165d49}code,pre{font-size:12px}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;background:#edf1e9;padding:18px}a{color:#315e50}details{margin-top:15px}summary{cursor:pointer} @media(max-width:800px){.split{display:block}.card{padding:18px}}</style></head><body><header><div><div class="eyebrow">THROUGH-TARGET-1.2 <span class="badge">PROVISIONAL</span></div><h1>Short plant. Direct chase.</h1><p>Current smooth running versus authored football redirects.</p></div><div class="headerlinks"><a href="./">Exact terrible-pass comparison ↗</a><a href="turns.html">24 interactive turns ↗</a></div></header><main>'''
page+='''<section class="card"><h2>The exact terrible pass</h2><div class="callout">The new runner brakes, plants and reverses over roughly one metre. He now reaches and receives the same ball at <b>5.8375 s</b>. The old path abandons at <b>1.0500 s</b>. Better movement makes this particular ball reachable; its success is not forced.</div><div class="split"><div><p>Same player A, starting at [28, 13.5] m and moving away at 6 m/s; same 45 m endpoint, 400 ms hold, Shot Power 99, Long Passing 1, Vision 1 and seed 22. The unchanged free ball ends at [38.2630, −15.3213] m when it slows to 2.5 m/s, then rests at [38.6824, −15.4893] m.</p><p>Use <b>Current + new</b> and <b>Focus on the initial turn</b> in the playable comparison. The old trace is grey; the new trace is yellow. The body arrow and foot marks show orientation during braking and the plant. The full-field view keeps the ball and meeting point visible.</p><p>Abandonment still works: both overhit and out-of-play fixtures release the run at 0.60 s. Future meeting estimates naturally receive a different runner position and velocity after the path changes.</p></div><div><h3>New path sequence</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Action</th><th>Time</th><th>Speed</th></tr></thead><tbody>'''+events+'''</tbody></table><p class="hint">Sprint event means 98% of requested pace; exact full pace follows. These are authored movement phases, with continuous velocity and position.</p></div></div></section>'''
page+='''<section class="card" id="measurements"><h2>All 24 corrections</h2><p>Every cell reads <b>current → new</b>. Each trial starts at the stated pace, facing along the initial velocity, with a fixed target 20 m away. Target replanning runs every 150 ms; movement steps at 240 Hz. Observation ends within 0.5 m of the target. All cases reached it.</p><p>Brake distance is travel before the first plant; “—” means no deliberate braking phase. Lateral excursion is maximum perpendicular departure from the direct start-to-target line. Facing requires body alignment within 10° of the current target direction for 0.10 s. “On new line” additionally requires velocity alignment within 10° and at least 90% of the requested pace, sustained for 0.10 s. Facing can occur during braking. Path/direct is travelled length divided by the actual direct start-to-finish distance.</p>'''+''.join(tables)+'''</section>'''
page+='''<section class="card"><h2>Movement model</h2><p>Corrections up to 30° keep the existing smooth running controller. Larger corrections reduce entry speed continuously with angle, brake along the incoming direction, hold a short support step while the body turns, then redirect and accelerate toward the updated target. Ordinary target refinements update the direction without restarting an ongoing plant. The player resumes the original running controller once aligned and back at pace.</p><p>A fixed neutral/high reference profile controls the redirect: braking 18 m/s², bounded redirect acceleration 22 m/s², push acceleration 9 m/s², maximum body turn rate 720°/s and angular acceleration 5,400°/s². The support step ranges from 35–90 ms and waits for body alignment within 20° before push-off. These are authored reference capabilities, not rigid-body football constraints.</p><p>The navigator accepts a separate movement-capability profile so Agility can later affect how quickly the redirect happens. No new Agility mapping is introduced. Existing Agility-dependent smooth running and RECEIVE behavior remain as before, and each runner’s sprint-speed limit is preserved.</p><p><b>Preserved prediction:</b> the existing meeting-point and feasibility solvers still use their original RUN forecast. This change replaces the executed approach path only. The 150 ms replans feed the runner’s new actual state back into those unchanged solvers; their future outputs and receive timings can therefore differ. Aligning the forecast with the new cut controller is outside this change.</p></section>'''
page+='''<section class="card"><h2>Passing scenarios</h2><p>These show the consequences of the changed route, with identical seeded ball launches, endpoints, selected players and rules. The difficult moving-target fixture takes longer with deliberate cuts; the terrible pass and runner-moving-away underhit become reachable.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Fixture</th><th>Current path</th><th>New path</th></tr></thead><tbody>'''+case_rows+'''</tbody></table></section>'''
page+=f'''<section class="card"><h2>Verification</h2><p class="tag">{v['checks']['passed']} checks passed · same-runtime deterministic repeats passed · all 24 turn cases reached the target.</p><p>The small 15° and 30° paths are unchanged. All 45–180° cases reduce lateral excursion. Checks cover mirrored turns, bounded velocity and body rotation, continuous root motion, repeated target refinements, exact current-baseline reproduction, unchanged ball flight before RECEIVE, no runner reassignment and the original abandonment hysteresis.</p><p>Hash comparisons passed for {preserved['protectedLabFiles']} existing lab files, {preserved['passingFiles']} approved PASSING-V1 files, {preserved['productionFiles']} production source files and all {preserved['receiveFoundationFiles']} RECEIVE foundation files. Frozen PASSING-V1 commit <code>{preserved['freezeCommit']}</code> remains unchanged. This candidate has not been approved or frozen.</p><p>The browser repeats the same complete replay exactly. Browser versus Node traces agree before RECEIVE to within 4.3 × 10⁻¹³ in the measured components, with the same 5.8375 s handoff. Their frozen RECEIVE continuations are not bit-identical: ball position differs by up to 0.242 m over the following two seconds. That receiving code remains untouched; this candidate does not claim cross-runtime identity after the handoff.</p><p><a href="browser-verification.json">Browser replay check</a> · <a href="validation.json">Validation evidence</a> · <a href="preservation.json">Preservation audit</a> · <a href="turn-study.json">Full turn traces</a> · <a href="run-terrible.json">Exact terrible-pass traces</a> · <a href="../through-target-1-1/">Previous lab</a></p><details><summary>Exact terrible-pass input</summary><pre>{esc(json.dumps(terrible['input'],indent=2))}</pre></details></section></main><footer>THROUGH-TARGET-1 remains provisional. Ready for owner visual review.</footer></body></html>'''
(p/'report.html').write_text(page)
print('Report written: 24 turn rows; 9 same-input passing comparisons.')
